From ceeee93aa77f0adc85de80185a50d08b7b0dfec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MoviePoop <dev@moviepoop.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:24:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: audio: drop frames whose channel count differs from
 the output

ConvertAVFrame() interleaves one plane per output channel, but the output
format is derived from the codec context while the frame is only checked
for a sane channel count. When FFmpeg returns a frame with fewer channels
than the context (seen with AAC in MP4 after seeking into damaged data,
right after "Invalid data found when processing input"), the interleave
reads frame->extended_data past the frame's planes and the decoder thread
crashes (SIGBUS in ConvertAVFrame on iOS).

Drop such frames and signal a discontinuity, as is already done for an
invalid channel count.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/audio.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/audio.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/audio.c
index e6c9128..b8f106b 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/audio.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/audio.c
@@ -458,6 +458,19 @@ static int DecodeBlock( decoder_t *p_dec, block_t **pp_block )
             if( decoder_UpdateAudioFormat( p_dec ) )
                 goto drop;
 
+            /* The output format is set up from the codec context, but
+             * ConvertAVFrame() interleaves the planes of this frame, one per
+             * output channel. After corrupt input (AAC in MP4, right after a
+             * seek) FFmpeg can return a frame whose channel count differs from
+             * the context's, and reading planes the frame doesn't have crashes
+             * the decoder thread. Drop such a frame. */
+            if( (unsigned)channels != p_dec->fmt_out.audio.i_channels )
+            {
+                msg_Warn( p_dec, "dropping frame with %d channels, output has %u",
+                          channels, p_dec->fmt_out.audio.i_channels );
+                goto drop;
+            }
+
             block_t *p_converted = ConvertAVFrame( p_dec, frame ); /* Consumes frame */
             if( p_converted )
             {
